Your API is Cute, But Where's the Real Backend? - Part 2 🤔 In Part 1, we ran the kitchen - took orders, routed them to the right chefs, and served our hungry users.
A guy in a stained T-shirt walks through the back door claiming he's "new kitchen staff." In a restaurant, identity matters. So does it in your backend. Think of JWTs (JSON Web Tokens) as guest passes. Without one, you're not getting a seat, let alone the special menu. 🧂 How it works: // User logs in → you give them a signed token { "userId": "12345", "role": "admin", "exp": 1724102400 }
// Client sends it in every request Authorization: Bearer <token>
// You verify it on every incoming request
